  "chain": "M&TE sensor improperly bonded to valve stem [cause TBD] -> erroneous low thrust reading on 1-1001-288 -> operator TS-required isolation of penetration X-0138 (closing/de-energizing 1-1001-298) -> both LPCI loops A and B inoperable for 21h14m [backups: High Pressure ECCS, both Core Spray loops available]",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Official cause_code is TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields (no letter code assigned in source header). Grease-quantity finding was initially suspected as a contributor but explicitly eliminated as cause per narrative, so not modeled as a failure mode. The 1-1001-298 actuator (Limitorque SMB-4) is cited in Component Failure Data as having 'failed to perform its design function when de-activated by operations' -- this reflects the deliberate operator de-activation, not an independent equipment failure, so no separate FailureMode node was created for it; it is captured via the isolation FailureMode and Component node. RHR containment spray/suppression pool cooling functions remained available but are not modeled as BACKED_UP_BY since they are different RHR functions, not LPCI backups per se -- only Core Spray and High Pressure ECCS are cited as coolant-injection backups to LPCI's core-cooling function."
}